  "outlook": "\u201cDemand for our products and aftermarket offerings remains high, with our order intake this quarter contributing to a backlog of $1.03 billion, an increase of 3% compared to last year,\u201d noted Sherman. \u201cWith our third quarter performance, our current backlog, and continued execution against our strategic initiatives, we are raising our full-year adjusted EPS* outlook to a new range of $3.30 to $3.40, from the prior range of $3.20 to $3.35. We are also narrowing our full-year net sales outlook to a new range of between $1.86 billion and $1.88 billion, from the previous range of $1.85 billion to $1.90 billion.\u201d"
